;">Trump, Xi, AI</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Last week, the world freaked out about an =
AI apocalypse. Now the two most powerful men, running the countries with th=
e two most advanced AI industries, are going to discuss that possible dooms=
day. Donald Trump and Xi Jinping are set to greet one another on Wednesday =
and meet for talks in Washington DC, and artificial intelligence will be hi=
gh on the agenda.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Though their meeting reflects concern for =
AI at the highest levels of government, which I think is a generally positi=
ve sign, early indicators are not signalling that either nation is willing =
to put regulatory checks on the technology. Both US and Chinese leaders hav=
e stressed in recent days that a slowdown of AI development is unnecessary.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99re leading China in AI=
,=E2=80=9D Trump said. =E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99re the most sophisticated countr=
y in the world, and frankly, I want to =E2=81=A0keep it that way, because w=
hoever wins AI, wins.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CFearmongering, confrontation and =
vicious competition will only disrupt the process of global AI governance,=
=E2=80=9D China=E2=80=99s foreign ministry said last week in a statement th=
at seemingly rejected the possibility of any US-led slowdown.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Any AI slowdown would need buy-in from the=
 US and China, but both rival nations see each other as the strongest argum=
ent against such a pause. Trump wants AI to go full steam ahead, fortified =
in that conviction by Silicon Valley leaders who=E2=80=99ve long been wary =
of Chinese ambitions. Even Dario Amodei, while calling for a global coordin=
ated pause, repeatedly called China a threat.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">China, meanwhile, sees the calls for a slo=
wdown as a way for the US to solidify American companies=E2=80=99 lead. Wou=
ld you accept a hobbling proposal from your first-place opponent?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">That doesn=E2=80=99t mean Beijing shares n=
one of Anthropic=E2=80=99s concerns.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Last week, China released the third iterat=
ion of its AI safety governance framework. Included in the updates are risk=
s posed by agents, cybersecurity threats from frontier models and the issue=
 of self-improving AI. Amodei has likewise highlighted risks on all three f=
ronts.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The combative stance between the trans-Pac=
ific rivals doesn=E2=80=99t mean nothing will happen, Trump=E2=80=99s admin=
istration is putting on a positive face in the lead-up to the meeting. The =
US treasury secretary, Scott Bessent, has already met with his Chinese coun=
terpart, He Lifeng, to discuss the threat of powerful AI. He called the tal=
ks =E2=80=9Cvery successful=E2=80=9D. Bessent and He mulled over an interna=
tional alert system for AI incidents in the same fashion as nuclear alert s=
ystems. The two delegations are set to<a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.t=
heguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR4TlkV015Ok9576v5vLffIx-ICLb-q=
yxXkUiOQn-4LXHX-8Vp_2YcP8Tod2CbeD0QfOUbx2dLjv1fmg-C4pDVB2BAtipkbnOTpVsfkib2=
Vpzfyyg-fEW2wdVtrxnv5OxZDmCANIC4ywUSfGlxXqLm3mlQRKdIZiNvgo_W2QjVK7U4THGrIaj=
AVBo0oMCwX9DjHVvonSRm82uVA2zTDm7fyhKh_Jc8MyemOE8G9lkjO_D5_WCadywKhU17GHKd6h=
u4cWEoLJKHSLIJgm1bpnwOlKCbdikz_ZKF54cGG8F4czs2K92dRkh6AIrITrKbtTBoA/4u9/xFL=
0NGw6ToubgMNOhI1e0Q/h14/h001.VxcZUigxUIohIFii9_foNWK47XIK5f_QAjNoAdmX-So" s=
tyle=3D"color: #0077B6;"> meet again in two months</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe US has proposed that we have =
a notification mechanism between the two countries, and we want a shared vi=
sion of common goals and common threats,=E2=80=9D Bessent said.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Read more: <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
